Basant Panchami, also known as Vasant Panchami, is a vibrant Hindu festival that ushers in the spring season and honours the goddess of wisdom, Saraswati.
For centuries, this festival has played a pivotal role in celebrating new beginnings, growth, and the pursuit of knowledge.
Students, artists, educators, and cultural enthusiasts alike look forward to this unique occasion, which not only marks the changing of seasons but also fosters renewal in life.
Basant Panchami is a festival deeply ingrained in tradition and spirituality, celebrated on the fifth day of the Hindu month of Magha, which typically falls in late January or early February.
The festival serves dual purposes—marking the onset of spring and worshipping Goddess Saraswati, the divine symbol of knowledge, wisdom, music, and the arts.

